[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4407036676","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119332#issuecomment-4407036676","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119332","id":4407036676,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBq4LBA","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-08T14:06:35Z","updated_at":"2026-05-08T14:06:35Z","body":"From what I've seen so far here, it's quite uncommon to have a PR build upon another PR. Especially since the change is completely independent, I would remove the 'quaternion rotation target' change from this PR.\r\n\r\nAPI wise, godot has created a distinction between 'spring' (position) and 'motor' (velocity) while in most physics engines it is part of the same thing. E.g. [HKR_physics_rigid_bodies](https://github.com/V-Sekai-fire/aria-forge-mcp/tree/main/thirdparty/glTF_Physics/extensions/2.0/Khronos/KHR_physics_rigid_bodies) uses: `stiffness * (positionTarget - positionCurrent) + damping * (velocityTarget - velocityCurrent)`. [PhysX](https://nvidia-omniverse.github.io/PhysX/physx/5.6.1/docs/Joints.html#drives) does the same thing. Since [this](https://github.com/jrouwe/JoltPhysics/commit/8ea82f777c409ffcfb7b9f4d29f3dc0df11faef7) change, Jolt does too.\r\n\r\nSo `G6DOF_JOINT_ANGULAR_MOTOR_FORCE_LIMIT` and `G6DOF_JOINT_ANGULAR_SPRING_MAX_TORQUE` is really the same parameter. One value is selected if the motor is in 'spring' the other in 'motor' mode. If in the future we want to support enabling both at the same time then it is unclear which parameter we would use. I'm not sure what would be the best way forward. It would break backwards compatibility to apply `G6DOF_JOINT_ANGULAR_MOTOR_FORCE_LIMIT` to the 'spring' mode, but I think it is the most appropriate thing to do (maybe with a project setting?).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4407036676/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4411908782","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119332#issuecomment-4411908782","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119332","id":4411908782,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBvhirg","user":{"login":"nikolay-egorov","id":28873057,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4ODczMDU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28873057?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov","html_url":"https://github.com/nikolay-egorov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-09T07:36:55Z","updated_at":"2026-05-09T07:36:55Z","body":"Agreed, I put the first commit for a clear diff only, will drop. \r\n\r\nRegarding api ambiguity, that requires some discussion beforehand. I'm not for carrying forward any technical debt in mental models. \r\n\r\nWhat seems reasonable to me is to keep both parameters: \r\n```\r\nG6DOF_JOINT_LINEAR_DRIVE_FORCE_LIMIT\r\nG6DOF_JOINT_ANGULAR_DRIVE_TORQUE_LIMIT\r\n```\r\n\r\nWe keep old params as aliases to the new api \r\n```\r\nG6DOF_JOINT_LINEAR_MOTOR_FORCE_LIMIT\r\nG6DOF_JOINT_ANGULAR_MOTOR_FORCE_LIMIT\r\n```\r\n\r\nHence, JoltGeneric6DOFJoint3D could now use unified storage, e.g., `double drive_limit[AXIS_COUNT];`\r\nHowever, a bit unclear what should be the default -- 0 or `FLT_MAX`? Latter seems a bit more correct to me\r\n\r\nThat said, I'm not familiar with the deprecation lifecycle in Godot, my suggestion would be: \r\nGodot 4.8 --> editor warning for `SPRING_MAX_TORQUE`\r\nGodot 4.9/5 --> `SPRING_MAX_TORQUE` removed. Let's not harden the burden of carrying legacy things forward\r\n\r\nProbably, the project setting might be: \r\n`physics/3d/joint_force_limits/legacy_split=true  # default false (new behavior)`\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4411908782/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4414818289","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119332#issuecomment-4414818289","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119332","id":4414818289,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABByTH8Q","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-10T08:17:42Z","updated_at":"2026-05-10T08:17:42Z","body":"> However, a bit unclear what should be the default -- 0 or FLT_MAX? Latter seems a bit more correct to me\r\n\r\nIf you pick 0 then the motor won't do anything (leading to many users spending hours wondering why the motor doesn't work). FLT_MAX should be the default.\r\n\r\n> G6DOF_JOINT_LINEAR_DRIVE_FORCE_LIMIT, G6DOF_JOINT_ANGULAR_DRIVE_TORQUE_LIMIT\r\n\r\nI think those are good names.\r\n\r\n> Hence, JoltGeneric6DOFJoint3D could now use unified storage, e.g., double drive_limit[AXIS_COUNT];\r\n\r\nThis cannot be unified while there's still the `physics/3d/joint_force_limits/legacy_split=true` project setting right?\r\n\r\nGiven that you came up with the `G6DOF_JOINT_ANGULAR_DRIVE_TORQUE_LIMIT` name, I think we could also do without a project setting:\r\n\r\n* `G6DOF_JOINT_ANGULAR_MOTOR_FORCE_LIMIT` will continue to set only 'motor' mode\r\n* `G6DOF_JOINT_ANGULAR_DRIVE_TORQUE_LIMIT` will set both 'spring' and 'motor' mode\r\n* Setting `G6DOF_JOINT_ANGULAR_MOTOR_FORCE_LIMIT` triggers a `WARN_PRINT_ONCE` that people should use `G6DOF_JOINT_ANGULAR_DRIVE_TORQUE_LIMIT` instead and explain that it operates on both 'spring' and 'motor' mode\r\n* At some point in the future we remove `G6DOF_JOINT_ANGULAR_MOTOR_FORCE_LIMIT` and unify storage\r\n\r\n(same for `LINEAR`)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4414818289/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4414917347","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119332#issuecomment-4414917347","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119332","id":4414917347,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABByZK4w","user":{"login":"nikolay-egorov","id":28873057,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4ODczMDU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28873057?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov","html_url":"https://github.com/nikolay-egorov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-10T09:11:24Z","updated_at":"2026-05-10T09:11:32Z","body":"> This cannot be unified while there's still the physics/3d/joint_force_limits/legacy_split=true project setting right?\r\n\r\nAgreed, that would make less hassle, the migration cost stays at the call site (where it's visible), not buried in project config.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4414917347/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4415219858","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119332#issuecomment-4415219858","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119332","id":4415219858,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABByrokg","user":{"login":"nikolay-egorov","id":28873057,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4ODczMDU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28873057?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov","html_url":"https://github.com/nikolay-egorov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-10T11:54:34Z","updated_at":"2026-05-10T11:54:34Z","body":"I've kept the quaternion commit so as not to cause any conflicts, as the test file was created in the first one","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4415219858/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4448473343","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119332#issuecomment-4448473343","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119332","id":4448473343,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCSZQ_w","user":{"login":"nikolay-egorov","id":28873057,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4ODczMDU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28873057?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov","html_url":"https://github.com/nikolay-egorov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-14T07:05:06Z","updated_at":"2026-05-14T07:05:06Z","body":"Cool! So I'll get back to cleaning up the branch after https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118997 is merged","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4448473343/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4450849747","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119332#issuecomment-4450849747","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119332","id":4450849747,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCUqT0w","user":{"login":"nikolay-egorov","id":28873057,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4ODczMDU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28873057?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov","html_url":"https://github.com/nikolay-egorov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nikolay-egorov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-14T12:56:04Z","updated_at":"2026-05-14T13:22:50Z","body":"Linux export project test failed with `ERROR: Cannot open resource pack '/tmp/test_project.pck` \r\nWhat could be the reason? \r\n\r\n**upd:** seems to be fine/flaky","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4450849747/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4454643189","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119332#issuecomment-4454643189","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119332","id":4454643189,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCYR19Q","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-14T20:53:27Z","updated_at":"2026-05-14T20:53:27Z","body":"@nikolay-egorov I've created a proposal for how this fits into the [bigger picture](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/14845). Note that I see this PR has been marked as 'Ready to Merge' for 4.8 so it will stay open until after 4.7 releases (same for the dependent change).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4454643189/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4458319376","h